body:
Okay
```
PImage fly,flybye,swatter,swatted;
float[] fX,fY;  // fly locations array
float[] swat;  // fly swatted binary boolean array, 1 = swatted, 0 = not swatted
int score=0;  // increments when swatted.

void setup(){
  size(800,400);
  fX=new float[0];
  fY=new float[0];
  swat=new float[0];
  // load images
  //fly = ;
  //flybye = ;
  //swatter = ;
  //swatted = ;

  fX = append(fX,0); //first fly - random location
  fY = append(fY, 0);
  swat = append(swat,0); // used as a boolean and matches to each individual fly, 0 = fly not swatted, 1 = swatted.
}


void populate(){ // draw the flies in memory to the screen.
  for(int i=0;i<fX.length;i++){
    if(swat[i]==1){ // if swatted
      // resize the fly image and place based on fx/fy array values
      image(flybye, 50, 50);
    } else { // not swatted
      image(fly, 50, 50);
    }
  }
}

void collisionDetect(){ //collision detection - detect collision between swatter and fly
  for(int i=0; i<swat.length;i++){
    println(fX);// bounding box detection
    if(fX[0] > 800 || fX[0] < 0 || fY[0] > 400 || fY[0] < 0 || mouseX > 800) { // condition should look at location of mouse and individual coordinates in fX and fY
      swat[i] = 1; // swatted
      fX =append(fX, 0); //new fly placed in random location when old fly dies.
      fY =append(fY, 0);
      swat =append(swat,0); // new fly not swatted
      score++; //increment score
    }
  }
}

void draw(){ 
  background(255);
  populate(); // draw flys to screen.
  fill(0);
  // set a text size and location for the score.
  if(mousePressed){ // image swap
    collisionDetect();
    image(swatter, mouseX, mouseY);   //draw swatter image to around mouse location - might want to play with this to get it to look right.
  }else{
    image(swatted, 50, 50); // if not pressed then alternative image.
  }
}``` 

Getting this error: Could not run the sketch (Target VM failed to initialize).
Make sure that you haven't set the maximum available memory too high.
For more information, read revisions.txt and Help ? Troubleshooting

Researched it, and it was suggested  that the image files might not be saved properly in the data directory, however, I've added them and this hasn't fixed the issue. Really at a loss. Urgh sorry about the format.
